Let $S\subset{\mathbb{R}}^3$ be a closed $C^2$ embedded surface bounding a convex body. At a point of $S$, the principal curvatures are the two eigenvalues of its shape operator. A point is umbilic when these eigenvalues agree, equivalently when the second fundamental form is a scalar multiple of the first. The question requires at least two distinct such points. \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]} \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0851}{[S2]}

